---
// <QuantPipeline> — the two deployment routes benchmarked in arXiv:2603.24607.
// Boxes and SVG arrows drawn from the theme tokens, like <PipelineFigure>: no
// image asset, no canvas, no library, nothing to animate.
//
// Flow: one trained float32 model forks into post-training quantisation and
// quantisation-aware training, both routes then pass through the SAME compiler
// before reaching the device. The compiler is drawn dashed because it is the
// proprietary step, and it is where the benchmark's largest losses appear.
//
// Column on narrow screens (arrows rotate), row from 900px up.
---

<figure class="quant">
  <div class="quant-flow">
    <div class="node node--io">
      <span class="node-title">Trained model</span>
      <span class="node-meta">float32</span>
    </div>

    <div class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">
      <svg class="arrow-glyph" viewBox="0 0 40 12"
        ><line x1="0" y1="6" x2="31" y2="6"></line><path d="M31 2 L39 6 L31 10 Z"></path></svg
      >
    </div>

    {/* The fork: two routes to the same 8-bit model. */}
    <div class="fork">
      <div class="node node--route">
        <span class="node-tag">PTQ</span>
        <span class="node-title">Convert, then calibrate</span>
      </div>
      <div class="node node--route">
        <span class="node-tag">QAT</span>
        <span class="node-title">Fine-tune, then convert</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="arrow arrow--labelled" aria-hidden="true">
      <span class="arrow-label">uint8</span>
      <svg class="arrow-glyph" viewBox="0 0 40 12"
        ><line x1="0" y1="6" x2="31" y2="6"></line><path d="M31 2 L39 6 L31 10 Z"></path></svg
      >
    </div>

    <div class="node node--opaque">
      <span class="node-tag">proprietary</span>
      <span class="node-title">Compile</span>
    </div>

    <div class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">
      <svg class="arrow-glyph" viewBox="0 0 40 12"
        ><line x1="0" y1="6" x2="31" y2="6"></line><path d="M31 2 L39 6 L31 10 Z"></path></svg
      >
    </div>

    <div class="node node--io">
      <span class="node-title">Edge TPU</span>
      <span class="node-meta">≈2 W</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <figcaption class="quant-caption">
    Both routes reach the device through the same compiler, and that is the step
    where the accuracy in the table below is lost.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .quant {
    margin: var(--space-4) 0 0;
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }

  .quant-flow {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: stretch;
    gap: var(--space-2);
  }

  /* ── Nodes ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .node {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2px;
    padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-3);
    border: var(--hairline) solid var(--border-strong);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    background: var(--surface);
    text-align: center;
  }
  /* What sits outside the conversion: the model going in, the device it lands on. */
  .node--io {
    border-style: dashed;
    background: none;
  }
  .node--io .node-title { color: var(--text-secondary); }
  /* The two routes carry the single accent, used as an indicator. */
  .node--route { border-color: var(--accent-line); }
  /* The step that cannot be inspected. */
  .node--opaque { border-style: dashed; }
  .node--opaque .node-tag { color: var(--text-faint); }

  .node-tag {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-label);
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .node-title {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }
  .node-meta {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-label);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  /* The fork holds both routes in the slot one node would occupy. */
  .fork {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2);
  }
  .fork .node { flex: 1 1 0; justify-content: center; }

  /* ── Arrows ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .arrow {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 6px;
    color: var(--text-faint);
  }
  .arrow-glyph {
    width: 26px;
    height: 10px;
    transform: rotate(90deg); /* column layout: pointing down */
    overflow: visible;
  }
  .arrow-glyph line {
    stroke: currentColor;
    stroke-width: 1.25;
  }
  .arrow-glyph path { fill: currentColor; }
  .arrow-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-label);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  .quant-caption {
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  /* ── Wide: lay the flow out left to right ──────────────────────────────── */
  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .quant-flow {
      flex-direction: row;
      align-items: stretch;
      gap: var(--space-1);
    }
    .node { flex: 1 1 0; justify-content: center; min-width: 0; }
    .fork { flex: 1.35 1 0; }
    .arrow {
      flex: 0 0 auto;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 2px;
    }
    .arrow-glyph { transform: none; }
  }
</style>
